MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am a little weak to bid this in real life. However, I will do it for teaching purpose. If I bid 4@D over a Weak-2 bid by East, that shows diamonds and hearts, at least 5-5 and is called ^*BLeaping Michaels^*n. You might ask, why not bid 3@S as |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=michaels,Michaels^*N|CP||FP||at| You could play that, but experts play 3@S is a stopper ask for 3N.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 27 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If you play Leaping Michaels, then you would bid 3@S when you have a hand with no spade stopper and either has a long running minor or is a strong balanced hand.|
PG| ***** 28 ***** |


mb|4D|an|D and H|
PG| ***** 29 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|4H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is the correct bid.|
